[
  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Review found 11 issues: 3 High, 6 Medium, and 2 Low. The binary builds, but ordinary regression probes exposed incorrect evaluation, formatting changes that alter behavior, and input-triggered panics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "All behavioral findings below were reproduced through the built CLI. Reachability through the public `just::run()` API was established by source inspection. No crate source files were changed; harnesses and generated justfiles are confined to `/work/tmp`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Formatting multiline module documentation corrupts valid source\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/item.rs:68](/work/crate/src/item.rs:68).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `--fmt` preserves a valid justfile\u2019s meaning and parseability.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: `[doc(\"first\\nsecond\")]` followed by `mod child` becomes:\n```text\n# first\nsecond\nmod child\n```\n`--fmt` succeeds and overwrites the file, but the next invocation rejects line 2. This can leave an ordinary project unusable after formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `test_format_multiline_module_docs_remains_valid` reproduced the successful write followed by a parse failure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "preserve the doc attribute\u2019s escaped string representation, or emit valid comments for every line while preserving the documentation value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning errors\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/function.rs:246](/work/crate/src/function.rs:246), [src/function.rs:250](/work/crate/src/function.rs:250), [src/config.rs:137](/work/crate/src/config.rs:137).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: malformed format strings produce actionable function or configuration errors.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: `datetime('%Q')`, `datetime_utc('%')`, and `--timestamp --timestamp-format %Q` each panic with \u201ca Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly\u201d and exit 101. The unchecked formatting error also escapes the public `run()` API.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: three executed regression cases reproduced these panics. Existing datetime tests cover successful formats only.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate Chrono format items or use fallible formatting, returning a normal diagnostic.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Ambiguous module directories outside the project cause a panic\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/compiler.rs:204](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:204).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: an ambiguous module source produces `AmbiguousModuleFile`, including useful candidate paths.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: with `mod child '../shared'` and both `shared/justfile` and `shared/.justfile` present, `just --list` panics on `StripPrefixError` and exits 101. Valid external module paths need not start with the importing file\u2019s parent directory.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `test_ambiguous_external_module_directory_returns_diagnostic` reproduced the panic.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "make candidate-path presentation fallible; retain absolute paths when stripping the parent prefix is impossible.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Formatting removes `eager` and silently skips required evaluation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/assignment.rs:7](/work/crate/src/assignment.rs:7).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: formatting preserves the existing guarantee that eager assignments run even with `set lazy`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: `eager x := \u2026` is rewritten as `x := \u2026`. An unused assignment that appended a marker before formatting stopped appending afterward, although the recipe still succeeded.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `test_format_preserves_eager_assignment` expected two marker lines across two executions separated by `--fmt`; only one existed. The existing eager-evaluation test does not format its input.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "serialize the `eager` modifier and add a regression comparing execution before and after formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Inherited bindings override current-module assignments during lookup\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:411](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:411).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: references resolve to the current module\u2019s assignments before inherited values or predefined constants.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "env with a fallback overwrites present but empty environment values. src/function.rs:297. env(key, default) treats a present environment variable whose value is the empty string as absent. With CONTROL_EMPTY set to an empty value, env('CONTROL_EMPTY', 'fallback') returns 'fallback', even though the documented contract only substitutes the default when the variable is not present. This prevents callers from preserving an intentionally empty process environment value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: when the parent exports `x := 'parent'`, and a child defines `a := x` and `x := 'child'`, running the child prints `parent child`. Similarly, `A := HEX` with `HEX := 'custom'` evaluates `A` to the predefined hexadecimal alphabet.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The evaluator checks recursively inherited scope values before evaluating the current module\u2019s declaration. Results can therefore depend on names, evaluation order, and which command selected the variables.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: both scenarios failed executed regressions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "distinguish local evaluated bindings from inherited bindings, and resolve current-module declarations before falling back to inherited values.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Reusing a module source conflates distinct module identities\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `mod a 'shared.just'` and `mod b 'shared.just'` create distinct module instances with their respective paths.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: a shared recipe printing `module_path()` prints `b` when invoked through either module. Invoking both recipes prints only one line because execution deduplication treats them as the same recipe. An `a::x` override was also ineffective.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `test_reused_module_sources_have_distinct_identity` expected `a\\nb\\n`; observed `b\\n`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "separate source-text caching from module instantiation, preserving module path and binding identity for each declaration.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "User-defined functions discard module bindings and invocation context\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: functions referencing module assignments use their established values and overrides; invocation-sensitive built-ins retain the current recipe context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed:\n- With `x=overridden`, a recipe prints `overridden original` for `x` and `f() := x`.\n- Referencing one backtick-backed global directly and through two function calls executes its backtick three times.\n- A function parameter named `x` changes the value of a separate global `y := x`.\n- In a dependency recipe, direct `is_dependency()` returns `true`, while a wrapper function returns `false`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: four executed regression tests reproduced these results. Functions are documented as unstable, but their documented module-assignment access still produces incorrect values.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "use the defining module\u2019s bindings and overrides, place parameters in a separate scope, and preserve invocation context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Relative and unnormalized search ceilings are ignored\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/config.rs:295](/work/crate/src/config.rs:295), [src/search.rs:196](/work/crate/src/search.rs:196).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: equivalent paths identify the same ceiling, enforcing \u201cDo not ascend above\u201d that directory.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: from a child directory, `--ceiling .` finds and executes a parent justfile. An absolute ceiling containing `child/../child` behaves likewise. The normalized absolute path correctly stops the search with \u201cNo justfile found.\u201d\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: executed regressions covered both ignored forms and the working absolute-path control.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "resolve and normalize the ceiling against the invocation directory before comparing it with searched directories. Apply the same handling to project-root discovery.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Formatting removes module and alias privacy\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/item.rs:59](/work/crate/src/item.rs:59), [src/alias.rs:41](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:41).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `--fmt` preserves `[private]`, including its effect on listing and completion.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: formatting removes `[private]` from modules and aliases. A previously hidden module and its recipes subsequently appear in `--list --list-submodules`; a hidden alias appears in listing output.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: separate executed regressions reproduced both changes. The existing private-module test explicitly disables round-trip checking; the general round-trip helper checks textual idempotence rather than behavioral preservation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "serialize privacy attributes and test discovery output before and after formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Strict Clippy fails on the supplied newer toolchain\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/alias.rs:17](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:17), [src/invocation_parser.rs:333](/work/crate/src/invocation_parser.rs:333), also lines 404 and 648.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: Clippy 0.1.99 rejects one `manual_assert_eq` occurrence and three `assert_is_empty` occurrences in `src/`; another occurs in supporting integration tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequence: the strict lint gate fails despite a successful build.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Required plus-variadic parameters allow zero arguments. src/invocation_parser.rs:201. The invocation parser treats all variadic parameter groups as optional. For a recipe gather +items with no default, just gather is accepted and runs the recipe with items bound to an empty string. This violates the documented one-or-more requirement for + parameters and allows an incomplete invocation to execute the recipe body.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: strict Clippy failed. Repeating it with only these two lints allowed passed the entire workspace.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "update the assertions. This is reported as toolchain compatibility debt, not a correctness failure or a demonstrated MSRV failure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Private-item rustdoc fails on malformed Markdown\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/lexer.rs:807](/work/crate/src/lexer.rs:807), [src/lexer.rs:824](/work/crate/src/lexer.rs:824), [src/lexer.rs:851](/work/crate/src/lexer.rs:851), line 852.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the strict documentation check can document private implementation items.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Observed: regex-like prose is interpreted as an unresolved intra-doc link and three undefined footnotes. With warnings denied, documentation generation fails.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: strict private-item rustdoc failed with four diagnostics. Strict public-only documentation passed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "render these patterns as code.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Verification\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Commands ran from `/work/crate` with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true`, and `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2`. Installed versions were Rust/Cargo 1.99.1, Clippy 0.1.99, and rustfmt 1.10.0.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `cargo build --locked --bin just` \u2014 passed.\n- `cargo test --locked` \u2014 513 unit tests passed; integration results were 1,240 passed, 5 failed, 8 ignored.\n- `bash /work/[tooling]/scripts/[tooling] --audit /work/crate` \u2014 formatting passed; Clippy and private rustdoc failed as described; tests repeated the same five failures.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -A clippy::manual_assert_eq -A clippy::assert_is_empty` \u2014 passed.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --all-features` \u2014 passed.\n- `python3 -I /work/[tooling]/scripts/[tooling] /work/crate` \u2014 completed; its 60 print-macro candidates reflect this application\u2019s CLI output and were not counted as defects.\n- `python3 /work/tmp/review_regressions.py` \u2014 15 regression tests produced 17 expected assertion failures reproducing the behavioral findings. Inputs and diagnostics remain in `/work/tmp/review-regressions` and `/work/tmp/regressions.log`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The five pre-existing baseline test failures were attributable to this environment:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- Missing `USER` and `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` caused two failures.\n- The sandbox permits writing a mode-0400 file, defeating `format::write_error`.\n- Creating non-Unicode directory names returns OS error 84, blocking two tests before they invoke the crate.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "After creating `/work/tmp/runtime`, this command passed 513 unit tests and 1,242 integration tests, with 8 ignored and the three filesystem-blocked tests filtered:\n```sh\nUSER=audit XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/work/tmp/runtime cargo test --locked -- \\\n  --skip format::write_error \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_invocation_directory \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_justfile_path\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`cargo +nightly-2026-10-01 miri test --lib` stopped because isolation disallowed `getcwd`. Retrying with `MIRIFLAGS=-Zmiri-disable-isolation` ended with exit 137 before completion; that result is inconclusive and is not evidence of a defect.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Final count: findings \u2014 3 High, 6 Medium, 2 Low. Coverage was native aarch64 Linux; MSRV 1.85.0 and other-platform checks were unrun because those toolchains/targets were unavailable. Library doctests are disabled by the manifest. No dedicated security assessment, exploit work, fuzz campaign, or stress testing was performed. Last `/work/clock` reading: 11.8324 active minutes of 45."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Found **8 issues**, ordered by impact on ordinary use. Seven behavior findings were reproduced against the unmodified binary; the eighth is specific to the installed Clippy toolchain.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Shared source files mix module identities and overrides.  \n   [src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Explicit empty recipe option values are replaced by parameter defaults. src/evaluator.rs:543. For a recipe declared with [arg('name', long='name')] and show name='fallback', invoking just show --name= loses the explicitly supplied empty string. The parameter default path treats an empty option value as a missing argument and binds 'fallback', so callers cannot intentionally clear a default through the documented --name=value syntax.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   The compiler caches parsed sources by filesystem path, although parsed sources contain module-specific paths and assignment identifiers. The documented module isolation requires each module instance to retain its own identity and values.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Reproduced with `mod first 'shared.just'` and `mod second 'shared.just'`, where `task` prints `module_path()`: running `just first::task second::task` prints only `second` once. The second invocation is incorrectly treated as already completed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Separately, when distinct module files both import `common.just`, overriding `first::x` also changes `second::x`. Callers reusing common definitions can silently skip work or apply configuration to the wrong module. Both cases are covered by the scratch regressions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Formatting removes `[private]` from aliases and modules.  \n   [src/alias.rs:42](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:42), [src/item.rs:59](/work/crate/src/item.rs:59)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Formatting should preserve the documented visibility behavior. Alias formatting omits its attributes, and module formatting ignores its `private` field.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Executed `just --list`, `just --fmt`, then `just --list` on private aliases and modules. Formatting succeeds, removes `[private]`, and makes previously hidden entries appear.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   The existing round-trip helper only compares successive dumps ([tests/test.rs:369](/work/crate/tests/test.rs:369)); that verifies idempotence after information has already been lost.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "User-defined functions ignore variable overrides and reevaluate module assignments.  \n   [src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226), [src/evaluator.rs:241](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:241)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Functions may reference assignments in their module, and command-line overrides should determine those assignments\u2019 values. Function evaluation instead creates a fresh root scope and an empty override map.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   With:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   ```just\n   set unstable\n   x := 'original'\n   f() := x\n   show:\n     @echo {{x}} {{f()}}\n   ```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   `just --set x override show` prints `override original`, instead of `override override`. The same problem occurs through `--evaluate`. Callers receive inconsistent configuration depending on whether they access a variable directly or through a function. This affects the explicitly unstable function feature.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Shell-format evaluation corrupts values containing `!`.  \n   [src/justfile.rs:323](/work/crate/src/justfile.rs:323)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Shell-formatted assignments should recreate the evaluated values when loaded by a shell. For `greeting := 'Hello!'`, `just --evaluate --evaluate-format shell` emits:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   ```sh\n   greeting=\"Hello\\!\"\n   ```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Executing that output with either `sh -c` or `bash -c` produces the value `Hello\\!`, including the added backslash. Both shell round-trip regressions fail.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   The existing test at [tests/evaluate.rs:264](/work/crate/tests/evaluate.rs:264) asserts the incorrect emitted text without checking the resulting shell value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Relative or unnormalized ceilings fail to stop justfile searches.  \n   [src/search.rs:196](/work/crate/src/search.rs:196), [src/search.rs:246](/work/crate/src/search.rs:246)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   `--ceiling` promises to prevent searching above the specified directory. Its path is compared directly against absolute ancestor paths without resolving relative paths or cleaning `..`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   From a child directory without a justfile, `just --ceiling .` finds and executes the parent\u2019s recipe, exiting successfully. Passing the child\u2019s absolute path correctly returns `error: No justfile found`. An equivalent absolute path containing `child/../child` also fails to constrain the search.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Callers using ordinary relative paths can unexpectedly run recipes from another project. The absolute-path control passes; the relative-path regression fails.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Invalid date formats panic instead of producing ordinary errors.  \n   [src/function.rs:245](/work/crate/src/function.rs:245), [src/function.rs:249](/work/crate/src/function.rs:249), [src/config.rs:137](/work/crate/src/config.rs:137)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0108",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Invalid user-supplied formatting strings should produce useful errors. These paths call Chrono\u2019s formatting implementation followed by `to_string()` without validating the format.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0109",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Executed all three cases:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0110",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   - `datetime('%Q')`\n   - `datetime_utc('%')`\n   - `just --timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0111",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Each exits **101** with `a Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly`, rather than an application diagnostic. The timestamp case prevents the recipe from running. Existing date and timestamp tests cover valid formats only.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0112",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Cross-module aliases disappear from listings or attach to the wrong recipe.  \n   [src/subcommand.rs:555](/work/crate/src/subcommand.rs:555), [src/subcommand.rs:568](/work/crate/src/subcommand.rs:568)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0113",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Public aliases should remain discoverable through `--list`. Listing groups aliases solely by the target recipe\u2019s basename, then associates them with recipes in the current module.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0114",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   With `alias shortcut := helper::task`, `just shortcut` executes successfully, but both default listing and `--alias-style separate` omit `shortcut`. Adding an unrelated root recipe named `task` causes the listing to label that root recipe with `[alias: shortcut]`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0115",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Callers either cannot discover the alias or receive misleading information about its target. Both variants were executed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0116",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The configured Clippy check fails on Rust 1.99.1.  \n   [src/alias.rs:17](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:17), [src/invocation_parser.rs:333](/work/crate/src/invocation_parser.rs:333)\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0117",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   `cargo clippy --locked --all --all-targets --all-features -- --deny warnings` fails on `clippy::manual_assert_eq`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0118",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Allowing that lint exposes `clippy::assert_is_empty` failures at `src/invocation_parser.rs:333`, `:404`, `:648`, and supporting test `tests/choose.rs:243`. Allowing both lints makes the full check pass.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0119",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   This blocks the project\u2019s lint workflow on the supplied toolchain. It does **not** establish a failure on the declared Rust 1.85 minimum version.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0120",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Cargo checks ran from `/work/crate` on aarch64 Linux with Rust/Cargo **1.99.1**, `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, and two build jobs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0121",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo build --locked --bin just` | Passed |\n| `cargo test --locked` | 513 unit tests passed; 1,240 integration tests passed, five failed, eight ignored |\n| `TMPDIR=/target/review-test-tmp XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/target/review-runtime USER=review cargo test --locked` | 513 unit and 1,245 integration tests passed; eight ignored |\n| Same environment, `cargo test --locked --workspace` | Passed; eight ignored |\n| `cargo clippy --locked --all --all-targets --all-features -- --deny warnings` | Failed as described above |\n| Same Clippy command plus `-A clippy::manual_assert_eq` | Failed on four `assert_is_empty` occurrences |\n| Same Clippy command plus both `-A clippy::manual_assert_eq -A clippy::assert_is_empty` | Passed |\n| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | Passed |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked --no-deps --all-features` | Passed |\n| `python3 /work/tmp/review/regressions.py` | 14 tests executed: 12 failures covering the seven behavior findings; two controls passed |\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0122",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The five initial integration failures were environmental: missing `USER` and `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, `/work` permitting writes to read-only files, and two non-Unicode directory-creation failures on `/work`. Local filesystem probes confirmed those differences; relocating temporary files to `/target` resolved them without source changes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0123",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "No production files were edited. Added fixtures, harnesses, and logs are in `/work/tmp`, with filesystem-check directories under `/target`. The [regression harness](/work/tmp/review/regressions.py) and [results](/work/tmp/review/regressions.log) preserve the reproductions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0124",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Coverage was Linux-only; the eight ignored tests, Rust 1.85, Miri, and other platforms were not tested. Rustdoc passed; doctests are disabled by the crate. The mdBook check was unrun because `mdbook` is unavailable. No dedicated security testing was performed. Last clock reading: **7.4498 of 45 minutes used**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0125",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Found **11 issues**: ten reproduced behavior defects and one toolchain-specific lint failure. `/work/crate` was unchanged; regression scripts, fixtures, and logs are under `/work/tmp`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0126",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "All behavior findings were reproduced through the CLI. Root-cause explanations below come from source inspection.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0127",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Formatting multiline module documentation produces invalid syntax \u2014 [src/item.rs:68](/work/crate/src/item.rs:68).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0128",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   A valid module declaration using `[doc(\"first\\nsecond\")]` should remain valid after formatting. `just --fmt` instead writes a comment containing `first`, followed by a bare `second` line. Formatting exits successfully, but the next `just --list` exits 1 with a parse error. Ordinary formatting can therefore leave the justfile unusable.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0129",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Formatting removes `eager`, silently changing execution \u2014 [src/assignment.rs:16](/work/crate/src/assignment.rs:16).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0130",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   With `set unstable`, `set lazy`, and `eager check := ` followed by the backtick command `exit 9`, invocation initially exits 9. After `just --fmt`, `eager` is gone and invocation exits 0. The existing `lazy::eager_assignments_are_evaluated` test establishes the intended behavior. Formatting can silently disable initialization or validation assignments.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0131",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Two module names loading the same file share an execution identity \u2014 [src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0132",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Given `mod a 'shared.just'` and `mod b 'shared.just'`, each module should retain its own path, scope, and recipe identity. With a shared recipe printing `module_path()`, `just a::show b::show` prints only `b`, exiting 0; expected output is `a` followed by `b`. The compiler caches the parsed source solely by file path, retaining one module context. A requested recipe is silently skipped; separate module overrides also interfere.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0133",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "References can ignore redefined constants \u2014 [src/evaluator.rs:411](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:411).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0134",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Constant redefinition is explicitly supported by `tests/constants.rs`. However, with `A := HEX` and `HEX := 'custom'`, a recipe printing both produces `0123456789abcdef custom`, rather than `custom custom`. Similarly, `just --evaluate z` for `z := HEX` returns the predefined constant despite the redefinition.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0135",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Lookup finds the inherited prelude binding before resolving the local assignment. Results consequently depend on assignment-name ordering and which variables are selected for evaluation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0136",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "`lazy` is controlled by the root module instead of each module\u2019s setting \u2014 [src/justfile.rs:187](/work/crate/src/justfile.rs:187).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0137",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   The README states that each module uses its own settings. A child containing `set lazy`, an unused backtick assignment running `exit 9`, and an unrelated recipe should run that recipe successfully. Without root-level `set lazy`, invocation exits 9.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0138",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   The reverse also fails: root-level `set lazy` suppresses the unused assignment in a child using the default eager behavior. This can unexpectedly execute expensive assignments or skip intended initialization.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0139",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Unused assertions are evaluated during settings analysis \u2014 [src/evaluator.rs:37](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:37).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0140",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   `set lazy` should skip unused assignments, and selective `--evaluate` already has tests establishing that unrelated assignments are skipped. Nevertheless, an unused assignment containing `assert('a' == 'b', 'unused')` prevents an unrelated recipe from running. It also makes `just --evaluate good` fail when `good := 'ok'`; even `--list` fails.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0141",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Settings analysis evaluates every assignment and immediately propagates assertion errors, before runtime selection can exclude unused variables.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0142",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Formatting removes private visibility from modules and aliases \u2014 [src/item.rs:59](/work/crate/src/item.rs:59), [src/alias.rs:42](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:42).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0143",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Recipe argument patterns accept partial matches of alternatives. src/pattern.rs:10. Pattern::is_match delegates directly to Regex::is_match, so an argument pattern such as dev|prod accepts a substring instead of requiring the entire argument to match. For [arg('mode', pattern='dev|prod')] on build mode, invoking just build xdevx or just build xprod incorrectly passes validation and runs the dependencies and recipe body, despite neither value being a permitted mode.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0144",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   `[private]` should continue hiding the same items after formatting. Executed before/after `--list` comparisons showed that `--fmt` removes the attribute from both module declarations and aliases. Previously hidden items then appear in listings.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0145",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   The existing round-trip helper at [tests/test.rs:335](/work/crate/tests/test.rs:335) checks dump idempotence, which cannot detect a modifier lost during the first dump.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0146",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Shell evaluation output changes values containing `!` \u2014 [src/justfile.rs:323](/work/crate/src/justfile.rs:323).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0147",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   For `foo := 'hello!world'`, `just --evaluate --evaluate-format shell` emits `foo=\"hello\\!world\"`. Sourcing that output in both `sh` and Bash produces `hello\\!world`, with an extra backslash.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0148",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Shell-format output should preserve the original value. The existing test at [tests/evaluate.rs:264](/work/crate/tests/evaluate.rs:264) asserts the incorrect escaped text without checking its interpreted value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0149",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "User-defined functions discard overrides and reevaluate module assignments \u2014 [src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226), [src/evaluator.rs:241](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:241).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0150",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   Functions may reference assignments in their module. With `x := 'original'` and `f() := x`, invoking `just x=override show` prints `override original`; both references should observe `override`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0151",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "   A second regression referenced one backtick-backed assignment directly and through two function calls. Its counter file recorded three executions instead of one. Each function starts with a fresh root scope and empty override map, producing inconsistent values and repeating external commands. These findings require the documented unstable function feature.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0152",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Invalid date formats panic instead of returning an error \u2014 [src/function.rs:245](/work/crate/src/function.rs:245), [src/function.rs:249](/work/crate/src/function.rs:249), [src/config.rs:137](/work/crate/src/config.rs:137).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0153",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "    `datetime('%Q')`, `datetime_utc('%')`, and `--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'` all exit 101 with an uncaught panic: \u201ca Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly.\u201d An invalid format should produce an ordinary diagnostic. A routine format typo instead crashes execution.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0154",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The configured Clippy check fails on Rust 1.99.1 \u2014 [src/alias.rs:17](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:17).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0155",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "    `cargo clippy --locked --all --all-targets --all-features -- --deny warnings` fails on `clippy::manual_assert_eq`, enabled by the package\u2019s denied `pedantic` group.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0156",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "    Repeating the command with `--allow clippy::manual_assert_eq` reveals additional denied `assert_is_empty` diagnostics at [src/invocation_parser.rs:333](/work/crate/src/invocation_parser.rs:333), lines 404 and 648, and `tests/choose.rs:243`. This is a confirmed failure with the supplied Clippy version; older toolchains were not tested.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0157",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The executed project checks used Rust **1.99.1**, Clippy **0.1.99**, and aarch64 Linux. Cargo build/test/lint/doc runs used `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`, offline dependency resolution, and two build jobs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0158",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "| Command | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo build --locked --bin just` | Passed. |\n| `cargo test --locked` | 513 unit tests passed; integration: 1,240 passed, 5 failed, 8 ignored. |\n| `cargo test --locked --workspace` | Same five integration failures; workspace execution stopped there. |\n| `cargo clippy --locked --all --all-targets --all-features -- --deny warnings` | Failed as described above. |\n| Same Clippy command plus `--allow clippy::manual_assert_eq` | Failed on additional `assert_is_empty` diagnostics. |\n| `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | Passed. |\n| `RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc --locked --no-deps --all-features` | Passed. |\n| `cargo test --locked --test integration parallel:: -- --ignored` | All three selected parallel tests passed. |\n| `python3 /work/tmp/review_regressions.py` | Three control methods passed; 15 regression methods produced 18 failure records, including subtests. |\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0159",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The five initial failures were environment-dependent:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0160",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "- `directories::runtime_directory`: `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` was unset.\n- `functions::env_var_functions_unix`: the test unwraps the unset `USER` variable.\n- `format::write_error`: an independent probe confirmed that this sandbox permits writing a mode-0400 file.\n- Both `non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_*` tests: directory creation itself fails with OS error 84, before invoking `just`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0161",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "This adjusted run passed **513 unit tests and 1,242 integration tests**, with eight ignored and three explicitly skipped:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0162",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "```sh\nUSER=audit XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/work/tmp/runtime cargo test --locked -- \\\n  --skip format::write_error \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_invocation_directory \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_justfile_path\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0163",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "The reproducible harness is [review_regressions.py](/work/tmp/review_regressions.py), with detailed results in [review-regressions.log](/work/tmp/review-regressions.log). Its fixtures retain command arguments, exit codes, stdout, and stderr.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0164",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Coverage focused on `crate/src/`, using documentation and existing tests as the contract. Other platforms, minimum-Rust compatibility, release-profile builds, Miri, book/site checks, and remaining ignored signal tests were not run. No dedicated security testing was performed. Last `/work/clock` reading: **8.97335 minutes used of 45.0**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0165",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "The review found findings: 2 High, 8 Medium, and 2 Low. The binary builds successfully, but local regression tests demonstrated formatting changes that corrupt or change justfiles, incorrect module and function behavior, and unexpected crashes. No production source files were edited.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0166",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0167",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Formatting multiline module documentation corrupts the justfile\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0168",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/item.rs:68](/work/crate/src/item.rs:68).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0169",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: `--fmt` preserves a valid module\u2019s documentation and produces a valid justfile.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0170",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Observed: `[doc(\"line 1\\nline 2\")]` followed by `mod foo` becomes:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0171",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "```text\n# line 1\nline 2\nmod foo\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0172",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed evidence: `--list` initially succeeded; `--fmt` returned success and overwrote the scratch fixture; the next `--list` failed with `Unknown start of token '2'`. An ordinary formatting operation therefore leaves a working file unusable.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0173",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "preserve the documentation attribute and its escaped string representation. Add a format-and-reparse test for multiline module documentation; the existing formatting test covers only a single-line comment.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0174",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Variable cycles through functions abort the process\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0175",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/assignment_resolver.rs:61](/work/crate/src/assignment_resolver.rs:61).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0176",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: circular variable dependencies receive a diagnostic, consistent with direct variable-cycle handling.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0177",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed input:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0178",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "```text\nset unstable\nf() := a\na := f()\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0179",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Observed: `just --evaluate a` overflowed its stack and terminated with SIGABRT. Source inspection shows that resolving a call checks its signature without following the function body\u2019s assignment dependencies.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0180",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Consequence: an accidental circular definition terminates the entire process, including an application using `just::run`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0181",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "account for function references during dependency analysis and guard recursive evaluation. Add direct and indirect cycles involving functions to the existing cycle tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0182",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0183",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Formatting removes eager evaluation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0184",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/assignment.rs:16](/work/crate/src/assignment.rs:16).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0185",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: formatting preserves the `eager` modifier.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0186",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed input used `set lazy`, `eager check := ` followed by the backtick command `exit 42`, and an unrelated `show` recipe. Before formatting, `just show` exited 42. After successful `--fmt`, the assignment lacked `eager`, and `just show` printed `OK` and exited 0.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0187",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Consequence: formatting can silently disable validation or required setup.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0188",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "serialize `assignment.eager`. Test recipe behavior before and after formatting; formatting idempotence alone misses this loss.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0189",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Modules sharing a source file acquire the same identity\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0190",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0191",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: modules declared with distinct names retain distinct module paths and overrides.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0192",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed fixture:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0193",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "```text\nmod a 'shared.just'\nmod b 'shared.just'\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0194",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "`shared.just` contained a recipe printing `module_path()`. Running `just a::show b::show` printed only `b`, instead of `a` followed by `b`. With separate overrides, the sole invocation used `b`\u2019s value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0195",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Source inspection confirms that compilation caches context-bearing ASTs solely by file path. Consequently, recipe deduplication also treats these distinct module recipes as identical.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0196",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "distinguish module instances from cached source text, including their logical module context. Add a shared-source regression test.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0197",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "User-defined functions discard module evaluation state\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0198",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226), [src/evaluator.rs:241](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:241).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0199",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: a function referencing a module assignment sees that assignment\u2019s evaluated, overridden value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0200",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed tests demonstrated:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0201",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "- With `x := 'original'`, `f() := x`, and `x=override`, direct access printed `override`, while `f()` returned `original`.\n- With `x := uuid()`, direct access and two calls to `f()` produced three different values.\n- An exported module variable was missing from a function\u2019s `shell()` command.\n- Inside a dependency, direct `is_dependency()` returned `true`, while a function wrapping it returned `false`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0202",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Consequence: extracting an expression into a function changes configuration values, repeats evaluation, and loses execution context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0203",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "share the module\u2019s evaluated bindings and overrides through a separate parameter scope, and preserve the relevant execution flags. Existing function tests do not cover these combinations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0204",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Shell-format evaluation changes values containing exclamation marks\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0205",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "[src/justfile.rs:323](/work/crate/src/justfile.rs:323).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0206",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Expected: shell-format assignments reproduce the evaluated values when sourced.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0207",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed evidence: `foo := 'hello!'` produced `foo=\"hello\\!\"`. Sourcing that output with `/bin/sh` yielded the literal value `hello\\!`, including the added backslash.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0208",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Consequence: callers importing generated configuration receive incorrect values.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0209",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "use shell quoting that round-trips values. The existing test at [tests/evaluate.rs:274](/work/crate/tests/evaluate.rs:274) asserts the incorrect text; replace or supplement it with a shell round-trip test.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0210",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Formatting removes alias and module privacy\n\n"
