  {
    "id": "P0219",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Executed evidence: from an empty child directory, `just --ceiling . show` found and ran the parent justfile, printing `PARENT`. Passing the child\u2019s absolute path instead correctly returned `No justfile found`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0220",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Consequence: callers can unexpectedly run a recipe from a parent project.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0221",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "resolve and normalize the ceiling against the invocation directory before comparison. Existing ceiling tests supply absolute paths only.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0222",
    "report": "D",
    "text": "Conditional expressions evaluate errors in the unselected branch. src/evaluator.rs:371. Conditional expression evaluation eagerly resolves both result expressions before choosing a value. As a result, value := if 'a' == 'a' { 'chosen-then' } else { error('UNSELECTED_ELSE') } fails instead of producing 'chosen-then'. This breaks justfiles that use a conditional to keep a failing computation out of the active branch.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0223",
